# LiveKit Watchman-only publisher

**Goal:** Keep Android LiveKit media publish tied to Watchman, not Copilot.

## Steps
1. Gate in `CaptureService.maybeStartLiveKit`: start only when `operatingMode == OperatingMode.WATCHER` and connected; otherwise `liveKitStreamer.stop()`.
2. Do not add Copilot LiveKit toggles (`copilot_live_stream_enabled` was removed).
3. Keep Connectivity probes, API token/session routes, WebUI subscriber, and `LiveKitStreamer` — they are shared.

## Gotchas
- UI “LiveKit Connected (N sessions)” is a probe/session count, not proof of publish.
- Watchman publishes automatically when Connectivity is connected; there is no separate Watchman LiveKit switch.

## What didn't work
- Starting LiveKit from Copilot (with a Copilot switch) while stopping it on Watchman — inverted product intent and left web live view dark in Watchman.
- Deleting the whole LiveKit stack (API/WebUI/Docker) when only the Copilot publisher path was wrong.
